<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
          http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
          https://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.23.xsd">

    <!--
      "Pravilo kraja putuje" — BLOK-HISTORY.md §5.5.

      A game of blok ends under one of two rules:

        * `dosta`  — the first side to reach the target wins, full stop;
        * `prolaz` — the side that crosses the target must have CALLED that
                     deal and passed it.

      Two series with byte-identical deals have DIFFERENT winners under the
      two rules. The stored `winner` is therefore not checkable by anyone
      reading the record later — not on the owner's profile and not through a
      shared link — unless the rule is stored beside it. So it is stored, in
      two places, for two different readers:

        * per GAME, inside `payload`, because the player may change the rule
          between games of one series and the detail view renders each game's
          own label ("Do 1001 · prolaz");

        * per SERIES, in this column, because the history LISTING must keep
          not reading `payload` (§3.1) and still has to print that label on
          every row. It carries the rule in force for the series as it now
          stands — the newest game's — exactly like `target` beside it.

      NOT NULL with a default rather than a nullable column: §5.5 makes the
      absence of the field mean `prolaz`, so a NULL would be a second spelling
      of a value that already has one, and every read would have to remember
      to coalesce it. The default also does the backfill: rows written before
      this changeset are `prolaz`, which is what §5.5 says a record without
      the field means.

      varchar(8) fits both words with one character to spare; the service
      never writes anything else, because §5.5's normalisation maps every
      other input to `prolaz` rather than rejecting it (a label on a record
      is not worth 400-ing an older client over).
    -->

    <changeSet id="2026-09-08-blok-session-end-rule" author="mrodek">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <columnExists tableName="blok_sessions" columnName="game_end_rule"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>

        <addColumn tableName="blok_sessions">
            <!-- 'dosta' | 'prolaz'. The DEFAULT is also the backfill for
                 every series stored before the rule travelled. -->
            <column name="game_end_rule" type="varchar(8)" defaultValue="prolaz">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </addColumn>

        <rollback>
            <dropColumn tableName="blok_sessions" columnName="game_end_rule"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
